      "id": "wuthering-heights-s040-p02084",
      "source_en": "1 (p. 41) curate: A curate is a low-ranking clergyman. A perpetual curate, on the other hand, is comparable to a vicar, or parish priest, in that he holds a living, or a post that provides revenues from an endowment. The curate to whom Nelly refers appears to be of the latter type. Emily Brontë’s father, Patrick, was perpetual curate at the Church of St. Michael and All Angels in Haworth from 1826 until his death in 1861.",
